import mundane theorem    stdlib/reasoning/modus-ponens

theorem implication-and-currying
  metamath    impexp
  note        To get c = 0 from both a = 0 and b = 0, take a = 0 first and
              then b = 0, and conversely.
  let a ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  let b ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  let c ∈ ℝ                                                           (H3)
  then (if (a = 0 and b = 0) then c = 0) ↔ (if a = 0 then (if b = 0 then c = 0))

1.  (if (a = 0 and b = 0) then c = 0) ↔ (if a = 0 then (if b = 0 then c = 0))
    both directions

    direction
    assume if (a = 0 and b = 0) then c = 0                            (D1)

    1.1.  If a = 0 then (if b = 0 then c = 0).
          proof
          assume a = 0                                                (K1)

          1.1.1.  If b = 0 then c = 0.
                  proof
                  assume b = 0                                        (K2)

                  1.1.1.1.  a = 0 and b = 0
                            join K1, K2

                  1.1.1.2.  c = 0
                            mun:modus-ponens, from D1, 1.1.1.1

    direction
    assume if a = 0 then (if b = 0 then c = 0)                        (D2)

    1.2.  If (a = 0 and b = 0) then c = 0.
          proof
          assume a = 0 and b = 0                                      (K3)

          1.2.1.  If b = 0 then c = 0.
                  mun:modus-ponens, from D2, K3

          1.2.2.  c = 0
                  mun:modus-ponens, from K3, 1.2.1
